      "source": [
        "# Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook, titled \"Holocron\", is an information retrieval system. Inspired by the ancient, knowledge-storing artifacts of the Star Wars universe, Holocron implements custom text preprocessing, lexicon generation, inverted and direct indexing, BM25 scoring, and Document-At-A-Time (DAAT) candidate traversal. Evaluated against the Vaswani corpus using standard TREC benchmarks.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key Features:\n",
        "- **Document Preprocessing:** Implements robust methods for cleaning, normalizing, and tokenizing documents to prepare them for indexing.\n",
        "- **Advanced Indexing Structures:** Constructs efficient data structures such as an inverted index, direct index, and lexicon to enable fast and accurate document retrieval.\n",
        "- **BM25 Scoring:** Utilizes the BM25 algorithm to rank documents based on their relevance to a query.\n",
        "- **DAAT Algorithm:** Applies the Document-At-A-Time (DAAT) approach for efficient query processing across large datasets.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8tgZDafi0c4e"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Dataset Overviwe\n",
        "\n",
        "**Title:** Vaswani Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "**Description:**  \n",
        "For this Information Retrieval project, I am using the Vaswani dataset from the ir_datasets collection. This dataset features a focused corpus of roughly **11,000 scientific abstracts** paired with natural language queries and corresponding relevance judgments, making it ideal for retrieval experiments in scientific literature.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset Properties:**\n",
        "\n",
        "| **Property**           | **Details**                                          |\n",
        "|------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|\n",
        "| **Documents**          | ~11,000 scientific abstracts                         |\n",
        "| **Queries**            | 93 natural language queries                          |\n",
        "| **Relevance Judgments**| 2,083 qrels (all labeled as relevant)                |\n",
        "| **Language**           | English                                              |\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset Structure:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Document Type:**  \n",
        "  - **GenericDoc:** A named tuple with fields:  \n",
        "    - `doc_id`: Unique document identifier  \n",
        "    - `text`: Full text of the scientific abstract\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Query Type:**  \n",
        "  - **GenericQuery:** A named tuple with fields:  \n",
        "    - `query_id`: Unique query identifier  \n",
        "    - `text`: Query text\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Relevance Judgments:**  \n",
        "  - **TrecQrel:** A named tuple with fields:  \n",
        "    - `query_id`: Query identifier  \n",
        "    - `doc_id`: Document identifier  \n",
        "    - `relevance`: Relevance label (1 indicates relevance)  \n",
        "    - `iteration`: (Additional field for iteration info)"
