    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lTUWtk2B-eN0"
      },
      "source": [
        "## **Index Construction**\n",
        "In this section, the `build_index` function constructs an **inverted index** and other supporting data structures for an **Information Retrieval (IR) system**. The implementation is **modular**, with clearly defined responsibilities across multiple functions to improve **readability, maintainability, and performance**.\n",
        "\n",
        "## **Overview of the Indexing Process**  \n",
        "The indexing process involves:  \n",
        "\n",
        "- **Lexicon Construction**: Assigning unique term IDs to words and tracking their frequency.  \n",
        "- **Direct Indexing**: Mapping documents to the terms they contain.  \n",
        "- **Inverted Indexing**: Mapping terms to the documents they appear in.  \n",
        "- **Document Statistics**: Storing document lengths and token counts.  \n",
        "\n",
        "This implementation efficiently processes a dataset containing **documents** (`docno`) and their **tokens** (preprocessed words).  \n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iuoDUEYr-zyl"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Initializing Index Data Structures**  \n",
        "### **Purpose:**  \n",
        "This function **creates and initializes** all required data structures:  \n",
        "\n",
        "- **`lexicon`**: Maps tokens (terms) to `[termid, document frequency, term frequency]`.  \n",
        "  - `termid`: A unique identifier for each term.  \n",
        "  - `document frequency`: Number of documents containing the term.  \n",
        "  - `term frequency`: Total occurrences of the term across all documents.  \n",
        "- **`doc_index`**: Stores document lengths as tuples `(docid, doclen)`, where `doclen` is the number of tokens in the document.  \n",
        "- **`direct_index`**: Maps document IDs to term IDs and their term frequencies.  \n",
        "- **`inv_d` & `inv_f`**: Store **inverted index** data:  \n",
        "  - **`inv_d`**: Maps term IDs to document IDs.  \n",
        "  - **`inv_f`**: Maps term IDs to their frequency in each document."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f7dxAmV8-c1z"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def setup_index_structures():\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Initializes the required data structures for indexing.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        tuple: Empty structures for lexicon, document index, direct index, and inverted index.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    lexicon = defaultdict(lambda: [0, 0, 0])  # [termid, document frequency, term frequency]\n",
        "    doc_index = []\n",
        "    direct_index = defaultdict(dict)\n",
        "    inv_d, inv_f = defaultdict(list), defaultdict(list)  # Inverted index storage\n",
        "    return lexicon, doc_index, direct_index, inv_d, inv_f\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tQ7hbMYe_OVv"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Lexicon Management**  \n",
        "### **Purpose:**  \n",
        "- Assigns a **unique ID** (`termid`) to each token.  \n",
        "- Uses `termid_counter` (a **mutable list**) to maintain a **global term ID counter**.  \n",
        "\n",
        "### **Why use `termid_counter` as a list?**  \n",
        "- Python **integers are immutable**, so they **cannot** be modified inside a function.  \n",
        "- Using a **list** (`termid_counter[0]`) allows modifying it **in-place**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h6QJZytx-cn5"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def update_lexicon(token, lexicon, termid_counter):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Updates the lexicon with a new token if it does not exist.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        token (str): The token to be added.\n",
        "        lexicon (dict): The lexicon mapping tokens to metadata.\n",
        "        termid_counter (list[int]): Mutable counter for term IDs.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        int: The term ID of the token.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    if token not in lexicon:\n",
        "        lexicon[token][0] = termid_counter[0]\n",
        "        termid_counter[0] += 1\n",
        "    return lexicon[token][0]\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Z4t-BkB-_fmj"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Processing Individual Documents**\n",
        "### **Purpose:**  \n",
        "- **Counts token frequencies** in the document using `Counter`.  \n",
        "- Calls `update_lexicon()` to assign a term ID.  \n",
        "- Updates the followings:  \n",
        "  - **Inverted Index** (`inv_d`, `inv_f`).  \n",
        "  - **Direct Index** (`direct_index`).  \n",
        "  - **Lexicon Statistics** (`lexicon`).  \n",
        "- Returns **document length** (`doclen`).  \n",
        "\n",
        "### **Data Structures Updated:**  \n",
        "- **`lexicon`**: Maps tokens (terms) to `[termid, document frequency, term frequency]`.  \n",
        "- **`direct_index`**: Stores term-document mappings.  \n",
        "- **`inv_d`**: Stores document occurrences per term.  \n",
        "- **`inv_f`**: Stores term frequency per document.  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KBSdE1cx_Zyz"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def process_document(docid, tokens, lexicon, direct_index, inv_d, inv_f, termid_counter):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Processes a single document, updating all index structures.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        docid (int): The document identifier.\n",
        "        tokens (list[str]): The list of tokens in the document.\n",
        "        lexicon (dict): Lexicon mapping tokens to term IDs and statistics.\n",
        "        direct_index (dict): Direct index mapping doc IDs to term frequencies.\n",
        "        inv_d (dict): Inverted index storing document occurrences per term.\n",
        "        inv_f (dict): Inverted index storing term frequencies per document.\n",
        "        termid_counter (list[int]): Mutable counter for assigning term IDs.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        int: The length of the document (number of tokens).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    token_tf = Counter(tokens)  # Count term frequencies within the document\n",
        "\n",
        "    for token, tf in token_tf.items():\n",
        "        token_id = update_lexicon(token, lexicon, termid_counter)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Update inverted and direct index\n",
        "        inv_d[token_id].append(docid)\n",
        "        inv_f[token_id].append(tf)\n",
        "        direct_index[docid][token_id] = tf\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Update lexicon statistics\n",
        "        lexicon[token][1] += 1  # Document frequency\n",
        "        lexicon[token][2] += tf  # Term frequency\n",
        "\n",
        "    return len(tokens)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "s5D21aWR_qbs"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Main Index Construction**\n",
        "### **Purpose:**  \n",
        "- **Initializes** all indexing structures.  \n",
        "- Iterates over each document using `tqdm` for **progress tracking**.  \n",
        "- Calls `process_document()` for each document's **tokens**.  \n",
        "- Updates **document statistics** (`num_docs`, `num_terms`, `num_tokens`).  \n",
        "\n",
        "### **Returns:**  \n",
        "- **`lexicon`**: Term metadata.  \n",
        "- **`inverted_index`**: `{docids, freqs}`.  \n",
        "- **`doc_index`**: Document lengths.  \n",
        "- **`direct_index`**: Term-document mappings.  \n",
        "- **`stats`**: Summary statistics.  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3eDE51eO-cjX"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def build_index(dataset):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Constructs an inverted index and other supporting structures from the input dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        dataset (DataFrame): A pandas DataFrame with the following columns:\n",
        "            - 'docno': Unique identifier for each document.\n",
        "            - 'tokens': List of tokens for the document.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        tuple: A collection of indices and statistics:\n",
        "            - lexicon (dict): Maps tokens to their metadata [termid, document frequency, term frequency].\n",
        "            - inverted_index (dict): Contains document IDs ('docids') and term frequencies ('freqs').\n",
        "            - doc_index (list): List of tuples (docid, doclen), where doclen is the number of tokens in each document.\n",
        "            - direct_indexfreqs (dict): Maps document IDs to term IDs and their term frequencies.\n",
        "            - stats (dict): Summary statistics.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    lexicon, doc_index, direct_index, inv_d, inv_f = setup_index_structures()\n",
        "    termid_counter = [0]  # Using a mutable list for consistent term ID tracking\n",
        "    total_tokens = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "    for row in tqdm(dataset.itertuples(index=False), desc=\"Indexing\", total=len(dataset)):\n",
        "        docid = int(row.docno)\n",
        "        tokens = row.tokens\n",
        "        doclen = process_document(docid, tokens, lexicon, direct_index, inv_d, inv_f, termid_counter)\n",
        "        doc_index.append((docid, doclen))\n",
        "        total_tokens += doclen\n",
        "\n",
        "    stats = {\n",
        "        \"num_docs\": len(dataset),\n",
        "        \"num_terms\": len(lexicon),\n",
        "        \"num_tokens\": total_tokens,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    return dict(lexicon), {\"docids\": dict(inv_d), \"freqs\": dict(inv_f)}, doc_index, dict(direct_index), stats\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8foIRAc5sDzb"
      },
      "source": [
        "## **InvertedIndex**\n",
        "\n",
        "The `InvertedIndex` class represents an **inverted index** used in information retrieval systems.  \n",
        "It allows **efficient document retrieval** based on term queries and supports the **BM25 ranking function**.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key Responsibilities\n",
        "- Stores the mapping of terms to documents (**Lexicon** & **Inverted Index**).\n",
        "- Manages document metadata (**Document Index**).\n",
        "- Implements **BM25 ranking** to score documents based on query terms.\n",
        "- Provides efficient **posting list iteration** for search operations.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Main Components\n",
        "- **Lexicon (`lexicon`)**: Maps terms to metadata like term IDs and frequencies.\n",
        "- **Inverted Index (`inv`)**: Maps term IDs to **posting lists** of documents.\n",
        "- **Document Index (`doc`)**: Stores document IDs and their lengths.\n",
        "- **Direct Index (`direct`)**: Maps document IDs to term frequencies.\n",
        "- **Statistics (`stats`)**: Stores global collection stats (e.g., total number of documents).\n",
        "- **BM25 Parameters (`K`, `B`)**: Used for document ranking.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ivdk_xSJIpdO"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Nested Class: `PostingListIterator`**\n",
        "The `PostingListIterator` class is **a helper class inside `InvertedIndex`** that iterates over a term's posting list.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why is this useful?\n",
        "- Allows **efficient traversal** of documents containing a specific term.\n",
        "- Computes **BM25 scores** for ranking documents.\n",
        "- Provides functions to **jump** to a target document efficiently.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Attributes\n",
        "| Attribute | Description |\n",
        "|-----------|------------|\n",
        "| `docids` | List of document IDs where the term appears. |\n",
        "| `freqs` | Term frequencies in each document. |\n",
        "| `doclens` | A dictionary mapping document IDs to document lengths. |\n",
        "| `N` | Total number of documents in the collection. |\n",
        "| `avgdl` | Average document length. |\n",
        "| `K, B` | BM25 parameters for controlling term saturation and length normalization. |\n",
        "| `pos` | Current position in the posting list. |\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BMOttfmVOhNS"
      },
      "source": [
        "####Methods\n",
        "\n",
        "## `docid()`: Get Current Document ID\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Returns the document ID at the current iterator position.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:  \n",
        "- `int`: Document ID.\n",
        "- `math.inf`: If the iterator reaches the end.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "###**`score()`: Compute BM25 Score**\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Computes the **BM25 relevance score** of the current document.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Formula**:  \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "BM25(i) = \\log \\frac{N}{df_i} \\times \\frac{tf_i}{K \\cdot ((1 - B) + B \\cdot dl_i / avgdl) + tf_i}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:  \n",
        "- \\( tf_i \\) = Term frequency in the document.  \n",
        "- \\( df_i \\) = Document frequency (number of documents containing the term).  \n",
        "- \\( dl_i \\) = Length of the current document.  \n",
        "- \\( avgdl \\) = Average document length in the collection.  \n",
        "- \\( N \\) = Total number of documents.  \n",
        "- \\( K, B \\) = BM25 parameters.  \n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:  \n",
        "- `float`: BM25 score.  \n",
        "- `math.inf`: If iterator reaches the end.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **`next(target)`: Move Iterator**\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Moves the iterator:\n",
        "- To the **next document** if no target is given.\n",
        "- To a **specific document ID** if `target` is provided.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Parameters**:  \n",
        "- `target` *(int, optional)*: The document ID to jump to.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Efficiency**:  \n",
        "If `target` is given, it **skips over documents**, making retrieval faster.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "###**`is_end_list()`**:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Purpose**:\n",
        "\n",
        "  - Checks if the iterator has reached the end of the posting list.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "###**`len()`**:\n",
        "**Purpose**:\n",
        "   - Returns the total number of documents in the posting list.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "y4dD9JpyTKhD"
      },
      "source": [
        "###**`InvertedIndex` Class Constructor**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Purpose:**\n",
        "Initializes an instance of the InvertedIndex class with the provided lexicon, inverted index, document index, direct index, statistics, and BM25 parameters (K, B).\n",
        "\n",
        "## Attributes\n",
        "| Attribute | Description |\n",
        "|-----------|------------|\n",
        "| `lexicon` | A dictionary mapping terms to metadata like term IDs and frequencies. |\n",
        "| `inv` |  An inverted index containing term IDs and posting lists (document IDs and term frequencies). |\n",
        "| `doc` |  A list of documents, each containing a document ID and length. `(docid, doclen)`. |\n",
        "| `direct` | Direct index: Maps document IDs to term frequencies. |\n",
        "| `stats` | A dictionary containing collection statistics like the total number of documents. |\n",
        "| `N` | Total number of documents. |\n",
        "| `doclens` | A dictionary mapping document IDs to document lengths. |\n",
        "| `avgdl` | Average document length in the collection. |\n",
        "| `K, B` | BM25 scoring parameters. |\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e_bS84-hUv5s"
      },
      "source": [
        "####**Methods**\n",
        "###**`num_docs()`**\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Returns the **total number of documents** in the index.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why is this important?**  \n",
        "- Used in **BM25 scoring** to compute the **inverse document frequency (IDF)**.\n",
        "- Helps in **normalizing** scores based on collection size.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:  \n",
        "- `int`: Total number of documents.\n",
        "\n",
        "###**`get_posting(termids)`**\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Fetches the **posting list** of a given term.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How does it work?**  \n",
        "- Looks up the **term ID** in `lexicon`.\n",
        "- Retrieves document IDs & term frequencies from `inv` index.\n",
        "- Returns a `PostingListIterator` for **efficient iteration**.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:  \n",
        "- `PostingListIterator`: Iterator for the posting list `list[PostingListIterator]`.\n",
        "- `[]`: If the term does not exist.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **`get_termids(tokens)`**\n",
        "**Purpose**:  \n",
        "Retrieves the term IDs for a list of tokens (terms).\n",
        "\n",
        "**How does it work?**  \n",
        "- For each token in the tokens list (of the query), it checks whether the token exists in the lexicon.\n",
        "-If found, it retrieves the term ID associated with the token.\n",
        "-Returns a list of term IDs for the tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:  \n",
        "- `list[int]`: A list of term IDs corresponding to the tokens in the input list.\n",
        "- `[]`: If a token is not found in the lexicon.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **`get_postings(termids)`**:\n",
        "   - Retrieves a list of posting lists for the provided term IDs.\n",
        "   - Returns a list of `PostingListIterator` objects, one for each term ID.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SIPfjNlZ48W3"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class InvertedIndex:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Represents an inverted index for document retrieval.\n",
        "\n",
        "    This class provides methods to manage the lexicon, inverted index, document index, and retrieval statistics.\n",
        "    It also supports BM25 scoring for ranking documents based on term relevance.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Attributes:\n",
        "        lexicon (dict): Mapping of terms to metadata (e.g., term ID, frequencies).\n",
        "        inv (dict): Inverted index containing 'docids' and 'freqs'.\n",
        "        doc (list): Document index containing document IDs and their lengths.\n",
        "        direct (dict): Direct index mapping document IDs to term IDs and their frequencies.\n",
        "        stats (dict): Index statistics, including number of documents.\n",
        "        N (int): Total number of documents in the collection.\n",
        "        avgdl (float): Average document length.\n",
        "        K (float): BM25 parameter for term frequency scaling.\n",
        "        B (float): BM25 parameter for document length normalization.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    class PostingListIterator:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Iterates over a posting list for a given term, supporting BM25 scoring.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Attributes:\n",
        "            docids (list): List of document IDs containing the term.\n",
        "            freqs (list): Term frequencies in each document.\n",
        "            doclens (dict): Mapping of document IDs to their lengths.\n",
        "            N (int): Total number of documents.\n",
        "            avgdl (float): Average document length.\n",
        "            K (float): BM25 parameter for term frequency scaling.\n",
        "            B (float): BM25 parameter for document length normalization.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        def __init__(self, docids, freqs, doclens, N, avgdl, k, b):\n",
        "            self.docids = docids\n",
        "            self.freqs = freqs\n",
        "            self.doclens = doclens\n",
        "            self.N = N\n",
        "            self.avgdl = avgdl\n",
        "            self.K = k\n",
        "            self.B = b\n",
        "            self.pos = 0  # Current position in the posting list\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "        def docid(self):\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            Returns the document ID at the current iterator position.\n",
        "\n",
        "            Returns:\n",
        "                int: The current document ID, or math.inf if the list has ended.\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            if self.is_end_list():\n",
        "                return math.inf\n",
        "            return self.docids[self.pos]\n",
        "\n",
        "        def score(self):\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            Computes the BM25 score for the current document.\n",
        "\n",
        "            Returns:\n",
        "                float: The BM25 score for the document, or math.inf if the list has ended.\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            if self.is_end_list():\n",
        "                return math.inf\n",
        "\n",
        "            tf_i = self.freqs[self.pos]\n",
        "            dl_i = self.doclens.get(self.docid())\n",
        "            df_i = self.len()\n",
        "\n",
        "            return 0 if df_i == 0 else (tf_i / (self.K * ((1 - self.B) + self.B * dl_i / self.avgdl) + tf_i)) * math.log(self.N / df_i)\n",
        "\n",
        "        def next(self, target=None):\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            Advances the iterator to the next position or to a target document ID.\n",
        "\n",
        "            Parameters:\n",
        "                target (int, optional): The target document ID to jump to. Defaults to None.\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            if not target:\n",
        "                if not self.is_end_list():\n",
        "                    self.pos += 1\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                if target > self.docid():\n",
        "                    try:\n",
        "                        self.pos = self.docids.index(target, self.pos)\n",
        "                    except ValueError:\n",
        "                        self.pos = len(self.docids)\n",
        "\n",
        "        def is_end_list(self):\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            Checks if the iterator has reached the end of the posting list.\n",
        "\n",
        "            Returns:\n",
        "                bool: True if the list has ended, False otherwise.\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            return self.pos == len(self.docids)\n",
        "\n",
        "        def len(self):\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            Returns the length of the posting list.\n",
        "\n",
        "            Returns:\n",
        "                int: The number of documents in the posting list.\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            return len(self.docids)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __init__(self, lex, inv, doc, direct, stats, k, b):\n",
        "        self.lexicon = lex\n",
        "        self.inv = inv\n",
        "        self.doc = doc\n",
        "        self.direct = direct\n",
        "        self.stats = stats\n",
        "        self.N = self.num_docs()\n",
        "        self.doclens = {int(doc_entry[0]): doc_entry[1] for doc_entry in self.doc}\n",
        "        total_dl = sum(doc_entry[1] for doc_entry in self.doc)\n",
        "        self.avgdl = total_dl / self.N\n",
        "        self.K = k\n",
        "        self.B = b\n",
        "\n",
        "    def num_docs(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Returns the total number of documents.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns:\n",
        "            int: Total document count.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        return self.stats['num_docs']\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_posting(self, termid):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Retrieves the posting list iterator for a given term ID.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Parameters:\n",
        "            termid (int): The ID of the term.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns:\n",
        "            PostingListIterator: An iterator for the term's posting list.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        docids = self.inv['docids'].get(termid)\n",
        "        freqs = self.inv['freqs'].get(termid)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return InvertedIndex.PostingListIterator(\n",
        "            docids=docids,\n",
        "            freqs=freqs,\n",
        "            doclens=self.doclens,\n",
        "            N=self.N,\n",
        "            avgdl=self.avgdl,\n",
        "            k=self.K,\n",
        "            b=self.B\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_termids(self, tokens):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Retrieves the term IDs for a list of tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Parameters:\n",
        "            tokens (list[str]): List of tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns:\n",
        "            list[int]: List of term IDs.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        return [self.lexicon[token][0] for token in tokens if token in self.lexicon]\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_postings(self, termids):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Retrieves the posting list iterators for a list of term IDs.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Parameters:\n",
        "            termids (list[int]): List of term IDs.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns:\n",
        "            list[PostingListIterator]: List of posting list iterators for the terms.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        return [self.get_posting(termid) for termid in termids]\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Aby6bo_WTX6C"
      },
      "source": [
        "# DAAT Algorithm\n",
        "\n",
        "The Document-At-A-Time (DAAT) algorithm processes multiple posting lists in parallel, advancing through each list simultaneously to identify candidate documents for multi-term queries. This approach allows for early elimination of non-relevant documents and minimizes unnecessary comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Support for Boolean and Phrasal Queries\n",
        "- Efficiency for skipping irrilevance Documents"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nZUjAuiiTjnL"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Components of DAAT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aygZXsuiqPMq"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Function: `get_min_docid`**\n",
        "In an inverted index, each posting list is constructed by scanning through the documents, typically in the order of document IDs. As a result, the document IDs in each posting list are stored in sorted order. This ordering is essential because it allows for efficient merging and retrieval of documents when processing queries.\n",
        "\n",
        "The `get_min_docid` function leverages the sorted order by iterating over each posting list iterator and retrieving the current document ID (using the `docid()` method) from those lists that still have pending documents. Because the posting lists are sorted, the smallest pending document ID among all iterators is chosen as the next candidate for processing.This mechanism enables a **single-pass traversal** of the posting lists, making the retrieval process efficient and ensuring each document is processed only once.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Parameters**\n",
        "| Parameter  | Type                              | Description |\n",
        "|------------|-----------------------------------|-------------|\n",
        "| `postings` | `list[PostingListIterator]`      | A list of posting list iterators, each providing access to a document list associated with a term. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Returns**\n",
        "| Return Type | Description |\n",
        "|-------------|-------------|\n",
        "| `int`       | The smallest pending document ID (`docid`) among the posting list iterators. Returns `math.inf` if all posting lists are finished. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Functionality**\n",
        "1. **Initialize `min_docid` to `math.inf`**: This ensures that any valid document ID encountered will be smaller than the initial value.\n",
        "2. **Iterate through each posting list iterator (`p`)**:\n",
        "   - If the iterator is **not finished** (`p.is_end_list()` is `False`):\n",
        "     - Retrieve the current `docid` using `p.docid()`.\n",
        "     - Update `min_docid` with the smaller value between `p.docid()` and `min_docid`.\n",
        "3. **Return `min_docid`**:\n",
        "   - If at least one posting list contains pending documents, the function returns the smallest `docid`.\n",
        "   - If all posting lists are finished, it returns `math.inf`, signaling that no documents remain.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Edge Cases Considered**\n",
        "- If all posting lists are **empty or fully traversed**, the function returns `math.inf`.  \n",
        "- Handles scenarios where some posting lists are **still pending while others are finished**.  \n",
        "- Efficiently finds the **smallest pending document ID** in **O(n) time complexity**, where `n` is the number of posting list iterators.  \n",
        "- This function is a key component in **merging multiple posting lists efficiently** for query processing in an **inverted index-based search engine**.  \n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qSmgqH3EUR8U"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_min_docid(postings):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Finds the smallest pending document ID (docid) among the provided postings.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        postings (list[PostingListIterator]): List of posting list iterators.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        int: The smallest pending document ID, or math.inf if all postings are finished.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    min_docid = math.inf\n",
        "    for p in postings:\n",
        "        if not p.is_end_list():  # Check if the posting list has not been fully traversed\n",
        "            min_docid = min(p.docid(), min_docid)\n",
        "    return min_docid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
