      "source": [
        "### **TopKPriorityQueue Class**\n",
        "\n",
        "The `TopKPriorityQueue` class implements a priority queue designed to maintain the top-k elements based on their scores. This data structure is essential for efficiently managing and updating a limited set of the highest-scoring items, commonly used in information retrieval algorithms like Document-At-A-Time (DAAT).\n",
        "\n",
        "## **Attributes**\n",
        "The following table describes the attributes of the `TopKPriorityQueue` class:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Attribute  | Type  | Description  |\n",
        "|------------|-------|--------------|\n",
        "| `queue`    | `list` | A min-heap that stores tuples of `(score, docid)`. The smallest score in the heap is at the root. |\n",
        "| `k`        | `int` | The maximum capacity of the queue, determining how many top items can be stored. |\n",
        "| `threshold` | `float` | The minimum score required for an element to be considered for insertion into the queue. |\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## **Methods**\n",
        "\n",
        "### **1. `__init__(self, k=10, threshold=0.0)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Initializes the `TopKPriorityQueue` instance with a given maximum capacity (`k`) and an optional threshold.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Parameters:**\n",
        "- `k` (`int`): Maximum size of the queue. Defaults to 10.\n",
        "- `threshold` (`float`): Initial threshold value. Defaults to 0.0.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **2. `size(self)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Returns the current number of elements in the queue.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns:**\n",
        "- `int`: The number of items currently in the queue.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **3. `is_eligible(self, score)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Determines whether a given score exceeds the current threshold and could be added to the queue.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Parameters:**\n",
        "- `score` (`float`): The score to evaluate against the threshold.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns:**\n",
        "- `bool`: `True` if the score exceeds the threshold, otherwise `False`.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **4. `reset(self, new_threshold=None)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Clears the queue and optionally updates the threshold.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Parameters:**\n",
        "- `new_threshold` (`float`, optional): If provided, updates the queue’s threshold to this new value.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Behavior:**\n",
        "- Resets the queue to an empty list.\n",
        "- Updates the `threshold` attribute if a new value is provided.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **5. `__repr__(self)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Provides a string representation of the `TopKPriorityQueue` instance for debugging and logging purposes.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns:**\n",
        "- `str`: A formatted string describing the queue's current state.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Example Output:**\n",
        "<6 items, th=4.0 [(4.0, 1), (5.0, 2), (9.0, 3)]>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### **6. `add(self, docid, score)`**\n",
        "**Purpose:**  \n",
        "Attempts to insert a `(docid, score)` pair into the queue. The insertion only occurs if the score exceeds the threshold.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Parameters:**\n",
        "- `docid` (`int`): The unique identifier for the document.\n",
        "- `score` (`float`): The score associated with the document.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns:**\n",
        "- `bool`: `True` if the item was successfully inserted, `False` otherwise.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Behavior:**\n",
        "1. If `score` is greater than `threshold`:\n",
        "   - If the queue has reached its maximum capacity (`k`), replace the root element (smallest score) using `heapq.heapreplace` if the new score is higher.\n",
        "   - If the queue is not full, add the new `(score, docid)` pair using `heapq.heappush`.\n",
        "2. Updates the `threshold`:\n",
        "   - If the queue is full, the threshold is set to the smallest score in the queue (`queue[0][0]`).\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## **Heap Behavior**\n",
        "The `queue` is maintained as a **min-heap**, ensuring that:\n",
        "- The smallest score is always at the root.\n",
        "- Insertions and deletions operate efficiently, maintaining the top-k elements.\n"
      ]
